        "heading": "Analysis",
        "body": "Report the missing-field rate, the exception rate, the unresolved count, and the age of open cases.\n\nSeparate observation from interpretation. A small easy sample is not evidence of a strong control.\n\nKeep case-level detail available for review. A summary chart without records cannot support a decision.\n\nDo not copy a value because it looks familiar. Reopen the source and record what changed. This applies to humanresourcesoutsourced-auditing-access-changes-around-policy-acknowledgment.\n\nIf the rule changes, keep the earlier classification and apply the new rule to later cases. This applies to humanresourcesoutsourced-auditing-access-changes-around-policy-acknowledgment.\n\nUse a short reason code for each exception. The code should describe the evidence problem, not the person. This applies to humanresourcesoutsourced-auditing-access-changes-around-policy-acknowledgment.\n\nKeep the policy acknowledgment queue separate from the general inbox. A queue without an owner hides the oldest item. This applies to humanresourcesoutsourced-auditing-access-changes-around-policy-acknowledgment."
